iterations.reply:
I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so it has no file-system or HTTP authority. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or calling the metadata service would need capabilities the node doesn't hold, and the world can't import them. If operations wants either, the graph needs to grant those capabilities explicitly, for example a logging or state interface and an `http-client` scoped to `metadata.internal.example`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The host channel stamps its own session identity and reports delivery;
        // we return that confirmation unchanged rather than fabricating either field.
        aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

